	<text xml:lang="la">
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>Salus plus quam maxima.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la">Tametsi sępius ad te dare literas, <persName ref="p495">Bullingere</persName> doctissime ac pientissime, <lb xml:id="p1z2"/>apud me decreverim, tamen semper negotiis tum <persName ref="p2411">principis</persName><note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" n="1">Pfalzgraf <persName ref="p2411">Ottheinrich I.</persName> <persName ref="p278">Bartholomäus</persName> war dessen Hofprediger.</note> illustrissimi tum religionis atque pietatis <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>hactenus impeditus fui.</s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la">Nam ecclesiae <placeName ref="l2477">Palatinae</placeName> iam pridem verbo viventis dei velut <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>immortali<note xml:id="fna" type="footnote" n="a"><hi>Vor</hi> immortali <hi>gestrichenes</hi> immortalis.</note> semine, ut ait Petrus<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2"><cit type="bible"><ref>1Petr 1, 23</ref></cit>.</note>, renatae dici non potest, quantis laboribus et sollicitudini<lb xml:id="p1z5"/>bus in dies gravarint me et omnes, quotquot hic in <placeName ref="l619">Boiorum</placeName> finibus Christum prędicamus, ut has<note xml:id="fnb" type="footnote" n="b"><hi>Nach</hi> has <hi>gestrichenes</hi> ips.</note> <lb xml:id="p1z6"/>ipsas ecclesias ceu novellas plantulas in tanta pseudoapostolorum turba<note xml:id="fnc" type="footnote" n="c"><hi>Vor</hi> turba <hi>gestrichener Wortansatz.</hi></note>, <persName ref="p8312">Cochlearum</persName>, Scotorum<note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3">Die Scotisten, Anhänger und Fortführer der Lehren des Franziskaners <persName ref="p18125">Duns Scotus</persName> (1265/66-1308). <persName ref="p278">Bartholomäus</persName> bezieht sich hier wohl allgemein auf die Scholastik; s. auch unten <ref target="file12003">Nr. 1956</ref>, Anm. 5.</note> <lb xml:id="p1z7"/>et aliorum monstrorum papisticorum, in puritate verbi et sacramentorum retineremus.</s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z8"/>Verum cum a te, vir doctissime, munere chartaceo, videlicet libro in <persName ref="p8312">Cochleum</persName> scripto,<note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4"><persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> Schrift gegen <persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName>; s. oben <ref target="file11885">Nr. 1839</ref>, Anm. 3.</note> sim dona<lb xml:id="p1z9"/>tus, negotiis omnibus sepositis, tametsi numerosissimis, facere amplius non possum, <lb xml:id="p1z10"/>quin tibi, etsi nihil dignum habeam, quod rescribam, tamen hoc qualicunque exiguo scripto <lb xml:id="p1z11"/>vel aliqua ex parte pro accepto benefitio gratias agam.</s>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la">Proinde animo grato a me accipito, quę <lb xml:id="p1z12"/>hic tibi scribo, ut vel sic petitioni tuarum literarum<note xml:id="fn5" type="footnote" n="5">Nicht erhalten.</note> satisfaciam.<pb type="edition" next="315"/></s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z13"/>Primum non erat opus a me paululum in literis progresso hoc iuditii postulare, num <foreign xml:lang="el">ἐν <lb xml:id="p1z14"/>τῷ ἀντιλέγειν</foreign><note xml:id="fnd" type="footnote" n="d"><hi>In der Vorlage</hi> <foreign xml:lang="el">ἀντιλεγεῖ̈ν</foreign>.</note> <persName ref="p8312">Cochleo</persName> satisfeceris.</s>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la">Etenim perlecto libro tuo sic mecum iudico: immundam <lb xml:id="p1z15"/>et tardigradam <persName ref="p8312">cochleam</persName><note xml:id="fn6" type="footnote" n="6">Die spöttisch gebrauchte Übersetzung des Namens <persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName>' als "Schnecke" („cochlea") geht zurück auf <persName ref="p1974">Luthers</persName> Schrift "Adversus armatum virum Cokleum" (<bibl source="b671">WA</bibl> XI 297, 21).</note> ita esse confutatam, ut vehementius a quoquam in ordinem re<lb xml:id="p1z16"/>digi non possit.</s>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la">Quia vero vanus iste homo iam dudum depuduit, certissimum est parare illum <lb xml:id="p1z17"/>rursus, quo in te retorqueat male sana et ineptissima, ut non dicam etiam impiissima scripta.</s>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la">Fortas<lb xml:id="p1z18"/>sis etiam et me cavillis suis tediosissimis turbare conabitur.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la">Nam satis prolixo encomio <lb xml:id="p1z19"/>in epistolari forma<note xml:id="fn7" type="footnote" n="7">Nicht erhalten.</note> ad <persName ref="p7579">illum Aichstetum</persName><note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" n="8"><persName ref="p7579">Moritz von Hutten</persName>; s. oben <ref target="file11883">Nr. 1837</ref>, Anm. 8.</note> usque (hic enim testudo<note xml:id="fn9" type="footnote" n="9">Die Bezeichnung <persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName>' als "testudo" („Schildkröte") geht zurück auf die oben Anm. 6 erwähnte Schrift <persName ref="p1974">Luthers</persName> (<bibl source="b671">WA</bibl> XI 295, 19. 22 und passim).</note> in collegio canonicorum, quod vocant <lb xml:id="p1z20"/>chorum S. Wilibaldi, latitat)<note xml:id="fn10" type="footnote" n="10">Zu <persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName>' Aufenthalt in <placeName ref="l133">Eichstätt</placeName> s. Remigius <hi>Bäumer,</hi> in: <bibl source="b641">TRE</bibl> VIII 143.</note> proprio nuntio librum tuum una cum epistola<note xml:id="fn11" type="footnote" n="11">Oben <ref target="file11916">Nr. 1870</ref> oder vielleicht <persName ref="p278">Bartholomäus</persName>' Brief an <persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName>, den er hier zusammenfasst.</note> ad ipsum conscripta <lb xml:id="p1z21"/>transmisi.</s>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la">Inter alia sic illum rogavi, ne Ismaelis, viri duri et ferocis, instar velit esse <lb xml:id="p1z22"/>contra omnes, ne rursus manus omnium sint contra eum<note xml:id="fn12" type="footnote" n="12">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Gen 16, 12</ref></cit>.</note>.</s>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la">Etenim si omnes viros doctos in se provoc<lb xml:id="p1z23"/>aret, vix uni<note xml:id="fne" type="footnote" n="e">uni <hi>korrigiert aus</hi> uno[?].</note> praesertim <persName ref="p495">Bullingero</persName>, nedum tot ac tantis viris non dico satisfacere, quin imo <lb xml:id="p1z24"/>nec respondere posset.</s>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la">Quocirca si <persName ref="p8312">Cochleus</persName> pro solita sua impudentia regereret, <lb xml:id="p1z25"/>utinam, si <foreign xml:lang="el">ἀντιλογιστέον</foreign><note xml:id="fn13" type="footnote" n="13">wenn du ... einer Erwiderung würdig hältst.</note> tam stolido asino dignum iudicaveris, illa tua secundaria scripta <lb xml:id="p1z26"/>principis illustrissimi <persName ref="p2411">ducis Otthainrici</persName> nomine in vulgus aedas,<note xml:id="fn14" type="footnote" n="14"><persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> Erwiderung erschien bereits im November 1544 und wurde tatsächlich <persName ref="p2411">Ottheinrich</persName> gewidmet (<bibl source="b286">HBBibl</bibl> I, Nr. 160).</note> oro, praefixa epistola, in qua prin<lb xml:id="p1z27"/>cipem commonefatias, ut ab huiusmodi insulsis hominibus sibi caveat aut non curet, quippe ad <lb xml:id="p1z28"/>nihil aliud quam ad concitandas seditiones utiles.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="14" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z29"/>Porro ubi lateat haec cochlea, supra parenthesi paulum demonstravi.</s>
					<s n="15" xml:lang="la">Sed quo<note xml:id="fnf" type="footnote" n="f">quo <hi>korrigiert aus</hi> quod.</note> certior sis, <lb xml:id="p1z30"/>ubi testudo sese contineat, en rudius, sed manifestius commonstrabo.</s>
					<s n="16" xml:lang="la">Est oppidum satis celebre.</s>
					<s n="17" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z31"/>Illic sedes est episcopalis.</s>
					<s n="18" xml:lang="la">Praeterlabitur fluvius dictus die <placeName ref="l2563">Altmüll</placeName><note xml:id="fn15" type="footnote" n="15"><placeName ref="l2563">Altmühl</placeName>.</note>, distans a <placeName ref="l337">Neoburgo Danubi<lb xml:id="p1z32"/>i</placeName><note xml:id="fn16" type="footnote" n="16"><placeName ref="l337">Neuburg an der Donau</placeName>.</note> duo miliaria.</s>
					<s n="19" xml:lang="la">Hic se condit cochlea.</s>
					<s n="20" xml:lang="la">Nomen oppidi <placeName ref="l133">Aichstet</placeName>.</s>
					<s n="21" xml:lang="la">Primum canonicus <placeName ref="l157">Franco<lb xml:id="p1z33"/>furti</placeName><note xml:id="fn17" type="footnote" n="17"><persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName> war im September 1518 zum Dechant des <placeName ref="l157">Frankfurter</placeName> Bartholomäusstiftes ernannt worden; s. Martin <hi>Spahn,</hi> <persName ref="p8312">Johannes Cochläus</persName>, Berlin 1898, S. 45. 50.</note> <placeName ref="l307">Mogunt[iam]</placeName><note xml:id="fn18" type="footnote" n="18"><persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName> verbrachte ein Jahr, 1525/26, in <placeName ref="l307">Mainz</placeName> an der Seite von Erzbischof Albrecht; s. <hi>Spahn,</hi> aao, S. 131f.</note>, hinc petiit <persName ref="p19058">Saxones</persName>,<note xml:id="fn19" type="footnote" n="19"><persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName> hatte seit 1528 bei Herzog <persName ref="p19058">Georg von Sachsen</persName> in <placeName ref="l121">Dresden</placeName> und von 1535 an als Kanoniker in <placeName ref="l1682">Meißen</placeName> gelebt; s. Remigius <hi>Bäumer,</hi> in: <bibl source="b641">TRE</bibl> VIII 142f.</note> inde se recepit in<pb type="edition" next="316"/> <placeName ref="l449">Slesiam</placeName>,<note xml:id="fn20" type="footnote" n="20"><persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName> war von 1539 bis 1543 Domherr in <placeName ref="l66">Breslau</placeName> (<placeName ref="l449">Schlesien</placeName>) und sollte als Vertreter des Bischofs am Konzil von <placeName ref="l1107">Trient</placeName> teilnehmen.</note> ducatum <placeName ref="l2449">Bohemiae</placeName>.</s>
					<s n="22" xml:lang="la">Iam ab episcopo <lb xml:id="p1z34"/><placeName ref="l133">Aichstetensi</placeName> huc ex <placeName ref="l449">Slesia</placeName> vocatus, fortassis, ut nascenti evangelio in <placeName ref="l619">Bavaria</placeName>, si saltem posset, <lb xml:id="p1z35"/>et rigationem et incrementum<note xml:id="fn21" type="footnote" n="21">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>1Kor 3, 6f</ref></cit>.</note> prohiberet.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="23" xml:lang="la" ana="farewell">His vale multum.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="24" xml:lang="la">Datum <placeName ref="l337">Neoburgi Danubii</placeName> anno domini <lb xml:id="p1z36"/>44. die Iacobi apostoli.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="25" xml:lang="la" ana="salute">Saluta nomine meo omnes ministros, praesertim familiarem fac aut mihi <lb xml:id="p1z37"/>aut principi <persName ref="p8049">Vadianum</persName>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="26" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z38"/><persName ref="p278">Adam Barptholomaeus</persName>, aulę ducalis <lb xml:id="p1z39"/>a concionibus <placeName ref="l337">Neoburgi Danubii</placeName>, <lb xml:id="p1z40"/>tuus in domino frater.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Adresse auf der Rückseite:]</note>
					<s n="27" xml:lang="la"><pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>Doctissimo atque pientissimo viro <lb xml:id="p2z2"/><persName ref="p495">Heynricho Bullingero</persName>, <lb xml:id="p2z3"/><placeName ref="l803">Tiguri</placeName> in <placeName ref="l862">Helvetiis</placeName> div<lb xml:id="p2z4"/>ini verbi praeconi <lb xml:id="p2z5"/>vigilantissimo, <lb xml:id="p2z6"/>domino et fratri meo valde observandissimo.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
		</body>
